+    def GetMissingDictionaries(self, result: Any, recurse: bool = False) -> None:
+        """``GetMissingDictionaries``: note in ``result`` - a ``THashTable`` ROOT fills in -
+        every class this class derives from or declares a member of that no dictionary of the
+        process describes.
+
+        ``ECont`` holds a ``vector<Elem>``: the vector is not emulated from a dictionary, so
+        ROOT reports it missing however well it can lay one out (roottest's
+        ``CheckMissingDictionaries``), and with ``recurse`` the classes those classes name are
+        looked into as well. A class of plain numbers and strings reports nothing, which is
+        what ``execNamingMatches`` asserts of one.
